{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "ms-mainframe-change-data-capture-v1",
  "title": "Mainframe change-data capture into Azure analytics and serving stores",
  "subtitle": "A change capture path moves mainframe or midrange updates over private connectivity into Azure event, database, and analytics targets. Synthetic Azure reference; no deployment is implied.",
  "description": "### Problem\nModernization and analytics programs often need timely copies of legacy records while avoiding repeated heavy reads against operational mainframe systems.\n\n### Flow and Azure mapping\nA source-side capture component reads transaction logs and stages changes. A replication service transports ordered change records across ExpressRoute or VPN to an Azure landing point. Azure Event Hubs can carry streaming updates; downstream consumers can materialize selected records into Azure SQL or land them in Data Lake Storage/OneLake for analytics. A mapping and validation layer adapts source formats and schemas before consumer use.\n\n### Trade-offs and assumptions\nThe Microsoft reference uses Precisely Connect for source capture, transport, and apply; Azure services alone do not automatically provide native mainframe log capture. This conceptual Azure-ready diagram therefore shows a generic, replaceable CDC connector as an external/partner component and highlights data consistency, schema conversion, initial-load coordination, replay, and source-system load as design decisions. It does not claim zero latency or exactly-once semantics.\n\nSource: [Microsoft Learn](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architecture/example-scenario/mainframe/mainframe-replication-precisely-connect).\n\n## Source provenance\n\n- Origin provider: Microsoft\n- Target: Azure conceptual adaptation\n- Primary source: [Replicate Mainframe Data by Using Precisely Connect](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architecture/example-scenario/mainframe/mainframe-replication-precisely-connect)\n- Reviewed: 2026-11-06\n\n## Catalog status\n\nThis is an original, editable Azure conceptual adaptation. It is synthetic reference material, not a deployed system, certified vendor architecture, or automatic deployment plan.\n\n## Mapping caveats\n\n- CDC capture is vendor- or source-specific; do not imply Event Hubs itself reads mainframe transaction logs.",
